# Accessibility

## Standards

Target WCAG 2.1 AA compliance.

## Rules

- **Semantic HTML**: Use `<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<article>`, `<section>` over generic `<div>` and `<span>`.
- **ARIA attributes**: Add `aria-label` on icon-only buttons, `aria-expanded` on collapsible sections, `role` when semantic elements aren't suitable.
- **Keyboard navigation**: All interactive elements must be reachable via Tab and activatable via Enter/Space. Custom widgets need arrow-key support.
- **Focus management**: Trap focus inside modals. Restore focus to trigger element on close. Use visible focus indicators.
- **Color contrast**: Minimum 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text. Never rely on color alone to convey information.
- **Screen readers**: Hidden content for screen readers uses `sr-only` class. Dynamic content updates use `aria-live` regions.

## Example

```tsx
<button
  aria-label="Close dialog"
  aria-expanded={isOpen}
  onClick={onClose}
  className={styles.Dialog__CloseButton}
>
  <CloseIcon aria-hidden="true" />
</button>
```

## Anti-patterns

- Click handlers on `<div>` or `<span>` without `role="button"` and `tabIndex={0}`.
- Missing `alt` text on `<img>` elements (use `alt=""` for decorative images).
- Disabling browser focus outlines without providing a custom visible indicator.
